## Code And Security Review

- Fresh independent subagent review dispatch in this continuation failed with `agent thread limit reached`; this is recorded as an environment limitation and is not counted as an independent pass.
- Local review covered scope isolation, RBAC, idempotency, optimistic concurrency, SQL parameterization, SQLite triggers/foreign keys, append-only render/generation/share/command facts, temporary URL expiry recovery, avatar consent and revocation, raw-SQL parity, normalized secret/path redaction, API/UI live wiring, and no external provider or NotebookLM side effects.
- Local scans found no C25 source use of real NotebookLM, media/avatar provider SDKs, MCP calls, credential reads, URL/PDF/Drive pulls, render execution, publish calls, external network side effects, `any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, or non-null assertion patterns.
- Scan hits were limited to negative test strings, migration rejection guards, loopback QA origins, and the shared migration loader's expected `readFileSync` call.
- Repository writes use parameterized SQLite statements and C25 migration triggers mirror repository checks for workspace/run scope, payload parity, append-only facts, command target binding, and unsafe normalized text rejection.

## Remaining Limits

- C25 does not integrate live NotebookLM, media generation, avatar generation, MCP, credential brokerage, URL/PDF/Drive ingestion, render workers, preview hosting, or publishing.
- Temporary URLs and share states are descriptor facts only; future live media stages need separate provider credential mediation, sandboxing, consent, rate limits, artifact writers, takedown/expiry jobs, and external side-effect receipts.
